   "type": "Control",
   "name": "Upstream Dependency Mapping",
   "amendmentRef": "AIDCF-007A-AMD-002",
   "applicability": "Applies to every in-scope Required Function. Depth beyond the boundary may be limited by provider disclosure; that limitation is recorded, not treated as not applicable.",
   "assessmentCriteria": [
    "Each Required Function has an upstream graph covering all dependency classes in AIDCF-003 that apply; classes judged not applicable are stated with rationale.",
    "Each dependency record has provider, type, strength, applicable states, owner and evidence populated, or the missing attribute is recorded as UNKNOWN.",
    "External dependencies are traced to the boundary exit point and to the first known shared upstream node (for example grid substation or transmission circuit, carrier point of presence, cloud region, identity provider tenant).",
